  "stimulus": "Short chart symbols and unambiguous tablature-derived fragments were read from each usable score. At 120 BPM each pair of successive labels occupies one four-beat bar; a final unpaired label occupies four beats. Single-bar fragments are repeated once to meet the normal three-second input minimum. Both practice styles use the normal drum, bass and chord mix and no count-in. These are printed-key synthetic controls with standardized timing; they do not measure performance on commercial recordings.",
  "counting": "all_file_renders counts each readable file in each style. unique_input_renders collapses duplicate symbol sequences within a style. unique_pcm_renders also collapses short fragments that become identical to a longer fragment after the single-bar repeat. These duplicates have identical reference timing and metrics. Every pair passed a sample-identical PCM SHA-256 check.",
